          "name": "probe-reads",
          "probe_reads": {
            "cluster_id": "{cluster_id}",
            "dbaas_engine_version_id": "{dbaas_engine_version_id}",
            "request_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "mysql-cluster-version-upgrade",
      "service": "database/mysql",
      "enabled": true,
      "heavy": true,
      "_note": "HEAVY 2026-07-16 (svccov-mysql session, owner-approved SCP_RUN_HEAVY): dedicated 1-cluster campaign for the version-axis + new-instance-ops gap keys that the main database-mysql-cluster lifecycle (always creates the NEWEST engine version) can never reach: mysqlupgrademajorversion, mysqlpatchminorversion, mysqlshowinstance, mysqlmanualbackup, mysqlexportlog. STRATEGY (live GET /v1/engine-versions 2026-07-16: contents[0]=8.4.7 id a3c1085292c24ca084bdac14a789c4b9 (newest 8.4 minor), contents[1]=8.4.6 id c76ea50f2f87480b9ee71a2f26ab6eae, contents[2]=8.4.5 id d2bbd9342e0948da804fbc99874af9a1 (oldest 8.4 minor), contents[3]=8.0.41 id 03cf36ee3162415e854c411e3690c85e (older MAJOR, major_version 8.0) -- ASSUMES this descending-by-recency order holds; re-derive indices from a fresh GET if a run shows a capture mismatch): create the cluster on the OLD MAJOR (8.0.41) -> mysqlupgrademajorversion jumps it to the OLDEST 8.4 minor (8.4.5, still 'behind') -> mysqlpatchminorversion then jumps 8.4.5 -> 8.4.7 (the newest) on the SAME cluster. This single create thus proves BOTH version-mutation endpoints where either alone would otherwise need its own cluster (previously-known blocker: resending the CURRENT software_version to /patch 400s 'Unpatchable version' -- confirmed AGAIN on today's run 20260716-181204-4912 mysql-cluster-subops-b -- because there was no OTHER minor in the same major to target; the fix is a genuinely different target, not a body-shape fix). MinorPatchRequest body CORRECTED here: {backup_before_upgrade: bool REQUIRED, software_version: string REQUIRED} -- api_bodies.json/request_example only shows software_version; the model schema (data/api_docs.json database/mysql/minorpatchrequest) has backup_before_upgrade as REQUIRED too, a docs-example/model mismatch. PatchRequest (major-version-upgrade) body: {dbaas_engine REQUIRED string, software_version REQUIRED string} -- dbaas_engine is NOT a literal catalog token, it's captured live from the cluster's OWN detail GET ($.dbaas_engine) so it can never drift from whatever the backend actually reports. mysqlshowinstance needs a path param instance_name (a NAME, not an id) -- captured from $.instance_groups[0].instances[0].name on the cluster detail. mysqlmanualbackup and mysqlexportlog take NO request body per the docs model (only path params) -- the sibling mysql-cluster-subops-guarded fragment's export-log step sends a start_dt/end_dt body that isn't in the documented model; kept broad expect_status here so either shape still counts as reached. mysqlexportlog log_type is a fixed enum (alert|audit|slow), NOT dependent on a registered log-export-config (registration is PF-blocked 500 ContactAdminForAssistance -- reconfirmed AGAIN today, run 4912 mysql-cluster-subops-a -- so a real registered config was never going to be available); 'slow' used directly as the literal path token. C-group (mysqlcreaterestore, mysqlcreateotherregionreplica, mysqlswitchovercluster) deliberately EXCLUDED: each needs its own extra billable cluster or an ha_enabled=true cluster (today's run 4912 shows switchover 404 'switchover-host.not-found' on a single-node cluster -- structural, not this lifecycle's target) -- left as a follow-up lever, not attempted here to stay in the session's single-cluster/time budget. Own dedicated VPC/subnet (10.142.0.0/20) so this lifecycle never contends with the main database-mysql-cluster or the subops-a/b fragments' shared 10.134/10.136 ranges.",
      "steps": [
        {
          "name": "create-vpc",
          "service": "vpc",
          "method": "POST",
          "path": "/v1/vpcs",
          "json": {
            "name": "regrvpc{unique}",
            "description": "API regression DBaaS version-upgrade",
            "cidr": "10.142.0.0/20",
            "tags": []
          },
          "capture": {
            "vpc_id": "$.vpc.id"
          },
          "expect_status": [
            200,
            201,
            202
          ],
          "cleanup": {
            "method": "DELETE",
            "path": "/v1/vpcs/{vpc_id}",
            "service": "vpc"
          },
          "adopt": "vpc"
        },
        {
          "name": "wait-vpc",
          "service": "vpc",
          "method": "GET",
          "path": "/v1/vpcs/{vpc_id}",
          "expect_status": [
            200
          ],
          "poll": {
            "field": "$.vpc.state",
            "until": [
              "ACTIVE",
              "RUNNING",
              "CREATED",
              "AVAILABLE"
            ],
            "timeout": 180,
            "interval": 10
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "create-subnet",
          "service": "vpc",
          "method": "POST",
          "path": "/v1/subnets",
          "json": {
            "name": "regrsub{unique}",
            "description": "API regression DBaaS version-upgrade",
            "cidr": "10.142.3.0/24",
            "type": "PUBLIC",
            "category": "PRIMARY",
            "vpc_id": "{vpc_id}",
            "tags": []
          },
          "capture": {
            "subnet_id": "$.subnet.id"
          },
          "expect_status": [
            200,
            201,
            202
          ],
          "cleanup": {
            "method": "DELETE",
            "path": "/v1/subnets/{subnet_id}",
            "service": "vpc"
          },
          "adopt": "subnet#db"
        },
        {
          "name": "wait-subnet",
          "service": "vpc",
          "method": "GET",
          "path": "/v1/subnets/{subnet_id}",
          "expect_status": [
            200
          ],
          "poll": {
            "field": "$.subnet.state",
            "until": [
              "ACTIVE",
              "RUNNING",
              "CREATED",
              "AVAILABLE"
            ],
            "timeout": 180,
            "interval": 10
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "find-engine-version",
          "method": "GET",
          "path": "/v1/engine-versions",
          "expect_status": [
            200
          ],
          "capture": {
            "engine_version_old_id": {
              "list": "$.contents",
              "where_prefix": {
                "major_version": "8.0"
              },
              "get": "id"
            }
          },
          "capture_soft": {
            "engine_version_top_software": "$.contents[0].software_version",
            "engine_version_mid_software": "$.contents[2].software_version"
          },
          "_note": "engine_version_old_id = the OLD MAJOR (8.0.x) via semantic where_prefix (robust to catalog reordering). engine_version_top_software/engine_version_mid_software use literal contents[] indices (live-verified 2026-07-16: [0]=newest 8.4 minor, [2]=oldest 8.4 minor) because there's no where_prefix+min_by support for non-numeric version strings in this engine -- if a future run's capture looks wrong, re-derive from a fresh GET /v1/engine-versions before trusting these indices."
        },
        {
          "name": "find-server-type",
          "method": "GET",
          "path": "/v1/server-types",
          "expect_status": [
            200
          ],
          "capture": {
            "db_server_type": {
              "list": "$.contents",
              "where_prefix": {
                "purpose": "general",
                "type": "Standard-1"
              },
              "min_by": [
                "cpu_core",
                "memory_gb"
              ],
              "get": "name"
            }
          }
        },
